   1: # family-experience-mcp-first-build - Work Plan
   2: 
   3: ## TL;DR (For humans)
   4: 
   5: **What you'll get:** A first working MCP server named `아이랑 어디가` that answers one parent job: "이번 주말 서울에서 4살 아이랑 갈 만한 실내 체험 3개만 골라줘." It will return three short, source-labeled candidate cards with age-fit reason, parent checks, and one next action.
   6: 
   7: **Why this approach:** Build one stable tool first, with deterministic fixture data before live API dependency, then add one official Seoul cultural-events adapter behind the same contract. This keeps the PlayMCP demo useful even if API keys are not ready, while preventing unsupported live/age-fit claims.
   8: 
   9: **What it will NOT do:** It will not build the pharmacy or baby-product concepts in this pass. It will not claim nationwide coverage, reservation availability, live freshness, or child suitability unless the source supports the claim. It will not submit for PlayMCP review or the one-time contest entry.
  10: 
  11: **Effort:** Medium
  12: **Risk:** Medium - the main risk is official event records having weak age/stage text, so confidence labels and safe fallback behavior are mandatory.
  13: **Decisions to sanity-check:** Default public name is `아이랑 어디가`; first live source is Seoul cultural events; fixture mode remains allowed and clearly labeled.
  14: 
  15: Your next move: start execution with `$omo:start-work .omo/plans/family-experience-mcp-first-build.md`, or ask for a high-accuracy plan review first. Full execution detail follows below.
  16: 
  17: ---
  18: 
  19: > TL;DR (machine): Medium effort, medium risk, new TypeScript MCP app under `apps/family-experience-mcp/` exposing one `find_family_experiences` tool with fixture-first data, optional Seoul adapter, golden-prompt QA, and PlayMCP temporary-registration readiness.
  20: 
  21: ## Scope
  22: ### Must have
  23: - New implementation lives under `apps/family-experience-mcp/`.
  24: - TypeScript MCP server using current MCP TypeScript SDK docs:
  25:   - server imports follow Context7-documented patterns: `createMcpHandler`, `McpServer`, Zod `inputSchema`, and Streamable HTTP client/server smoke.
  26:   - endpoint path is `/mcp`.
  27:   - server name is `family-experience-mcp`; public display name is `아이랑 어디가`.
  28: - Exactly one public MCP tool in the first build:
  29:   - `find_family_experiences(location, child_age?, child_stage?, date_range, indoor_outdoor?, budget?, must_have?, max_distance_hint?)`.
  30:   - Require `location`, `date_range`, and one of `child_age` or `child_stage`.
  31:   - `location` may be a city, district, or compact Korean place phrase.
  32:   - `date_range` accepts natural labels used by golden prompts (`today`, `weekend`, `this_saturday`, or explicit ISO date range) plus a raw text field.
  33: - Structured output contains:
  34:   - `query`.
  35:   - `results` with maximum three candidates.
  36:   - `warnings`.
  37:   - `source_summary`.
  38:   - `next_action`.
  39:   - `mode`: `fixture`, `live`, or `mixed`.
  40: - Every candidate contains:
  41:   - `title`, `date_time`, `venue`, `address`, `age_fit_label`, `age_fit_reason`, `indoor_outdoor`, `fee_text`, `reservation_url`, `contact`, `source_name`, `source_url`, `retrieved_at`, `confidence`, `parent_check`, `next_action`.
  42: - Confidence labels are limited to:
  43:   - `source-stated`
  44:   - `computed`
  45:   - `inferred`
  46:   - `unknown`
  47:   - `stale`
  48: - Data pipeline stages:
  49:   - source registry.
  50:   - adapter boundary.
  51:   - raw snapshot / fixture id.
  52:   - normalizer.
  53:   - child-fit and practicality ranking.
  54:   - response renderer.
  55:   - typed failures.
  56: - Data sources:
